  "body": "# CREXX Dev Snapshot 20260917T173829Z\n\nThis is the latest successful build from the `develop` branch.\nIt is replaced by the next successful `develop` build and is not a versioned release.\n\n- Version: `crexx-1.0.0-beta.3+dev-snapshot.gd0feda283857`\n- Commit: `d0feda283857e9470e21fc143f8e2f70fa54ab3b`\n- Built: `20260917T173829Z`\n- Workflow run: https://github.com/adesutherland/CREXX/actions/runs/35253939469\n\nCore downloads contain cREXX. For local inference, add the matching llama.rexx platform/backend ZIP and download a supported model separately. One MSVC Windows core supports either Vulkan or CUDA. MinGW is a core quality gate only.\n\nmacOS .pkg assets, when present, are signed, notarized, stapled installers. macOS ZIP assets remain portable archives.\nWindows testers: use `CREXX-dev-snapshot-windows-x64-unsigned-setup.exe` for installation, or `CREXX-dev-snapshot-windows-x64.zip` as the portable archive. Both are built automatically from commit `d0feda283857`. Unsigned applications may show Windows security warnings or be blocked by policy.\n\nAdd local inference with `llama.rexx-dev-snapshot-windows-x64-vulkan-unsigned-setup.exe` after installing the matching core. Its install, provider, reinstall and removal checks pass before publication.\n\nOptional signed core and llama Vulkan ZIPs and setup executables are added together when the maintainer runs `scripts/sign-windows-dev-snapshot.sh`. Payloads, embedded uninstallers and setups are signed. Unsigned downloads remain available. Previous signed assets and legacy installers are removed whenever the snapshot is refreshed.\n\n### Automatic asset SHA-256 checksums\n\n```text\nedc748f8eaec9dbe1dba3239ff5f71d38b89cfe4e97d04a1ca6fc3e0b42cd97f  CREXX-dev-snapshot-linux-x64.deb\n4de90bb9a3d76e6032619b1c0fc866f881bfaf953127e87f2738ea1a63cc8422  CREXX-dev-snapshot-linux-x64.zip\n4df5a26d6f69355b6fc130521a6522e703f1f907a6e844b3cc0f1f4036a3afe7  CREXX-dev-snapshot-macos-arm64.pkg\ndc8a741ccac10bd104ae3c